	title: "Agi's Classes - Gourmet",
	text: 
"<font color=\"#f1a150\"><strong>Gourmet Cooking</font></color>

So, ya think you have what it takes to make Gourmet food do-ya?, well, you do, because it's rather simple.

To start, gather a few Flowers and Mushrooms, you'll need two of each at minimum, <font color=\"#f1a150\">All four must be unique!</font></color>. As you are an expert in the culinary arts, you can process any Flower and Mushroom, even if it's poisonous, into the most <a href=\"handbooksearch://Delectable Spices\">Delectable Spices</a>

To process them into a Spice, you also need a <a href=\"handbooksearch://Mortar and Pestle\">Mortar and Pestle</a>. You can make a Pestle by Knapping.

<font color=\"#f1a150\">But Wait!</font>

You can also combine them with any Crop to further enhance their flavor and nutrition. Try making some <a href=\"handbooksearch://Gourmet Spice\">Gourmet Spices</a>

These Spices can be used in Meaty Stews, Vegetable Stews, Soup, Scrambled Eggs, and even Porridge!

Gourmet Spices count as Vegetables for nutrition, and typically provide around twice the value of the Vegetable you combine them with, meaning they're a direct improvement. Additionally, Spices take a very long time to Spoil.

Spices provide no Nutritional value when eaten raw, thus it is important to use them if you got'em, as they have no value unless they're cooked into a meal. And as Chef Gusto said, 'Anyone Can Cook!' and thus, any class can cook a meal using the spices if they're available.

Cooking rules have not been changed, simply added to, the following will describe how to cook your favorite meals using Spices.
<font color=\"#db4646\"><strong>Meaty Stew</font></color>
Third and/or Fourth slot, maximum of 2.</font>
<font color=\"#cf73e5\"><strong>Porridge</font></color>
Third and/or Fourth slot, maximum of 2.</font>
<font color=\"#66db46\"><strong>Vegetable Stew</font></color>
Third or Fourth slot, maximum of 1.</font>
<font color=\"#96d4e5\"><strong>Soup</font></color>
Third or Fourth slot, maximum of 1.</font>
<font color=\"#f1a150\"><strong>Scrambled Eggs</font></color>
Third or Fourth slot, maximum of 1.</font>

You may have noticed that your Alchemist friends can help you make Food! You can use <a href=\"handbooksearch://Callahan Powder\">Callahan</a> and <a href=\"handbooksearch://Callahan Powder\">Holland</a> Powder to make spices in the place of the typical Vegetable compliment.

Alchemical Powders have the odd trait of being absorbed as Dairy. <a href=\"handbooksearch://Callahan Powder\">Callahan Powder</a> provides very mild nutrition, yet boasts healing properties. <a href=\"handbooksearch://Holland Powder\">Holland</a> however provides a large amount of Dairy Nutrition but is moderately toxic in the short term.

<font color=\"#f1a150\"><strong>Note</font></color> Health gained or lost by Alchemic Foods is relative to the amount consumed, such that eating half a serving will confer only half of the health modification.

<font color=\"#f1a150\"><strong>Enjoy your most <i>Delectable<i> Meals</font></color>
"
